# HARNESS EVALUATION LOOP

This loop is separate from task evaluation. It measures whether the harness improves on baseline. The automatic path opens only when the deterministic checker returns `targeted|full`.

## Entry routing

1. Freeze checker JSON at `evaluation/runs/<run-id>/trigger.json`. For an explicit full request, preserve the entire raw checker JSON in `override.original`; use effective top-level `decision: full`, `mandatory: false`; set `override.kind: explicit-user-request`; set `reasons: [*original.reasons, explicit-user-request]`; and preserve the original deferred reasons, hashes, and `acknowledgement`. Use raw checker full output without a wrapper. Reject simple decision edits and unstructured budget or cooldown bypasses.
2. If `reasons` contains `input-invalid:*`, do not open effect evaluation or an LLM judge. Run `{{SKILL_NAME}}-verify`, repair the structure, then rerun the checker.
3. If `adapter-change` or `parity-fail` is present, require provider parity first. On failure, add `parity-fail` once to `state/self-evaluation.json.pending_events`, then stop.
4. For `targeted`, run only deterministic metrics mapped to the exact reason in `evaluation/suites/targeted.json`. Do not add arbitrary scope or LLM evaluation beyond `cost-regression`, `retry-pressure`, and `deterministic-sample`.
5. Only `full` runs every comparison arm below.

## Comparison arms

| Arm | Condition | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| baseline | No harness | Measure the original runtime |
| control | Generic minimal instructions | Isolate simple prompting effects |
| treatment | Current harness | Measure harness-specific effects |

Use the same commit, fixture, model/version, permissions, tools, and budget for every arm. The linked evaluator has `scope: harness`, `type: experiment`.

## Procedure

1. FREEZE — Fix the suite, fixture, evaluator, and environment hash before execution.
2. RUN — Preserve raw targeted-metric or full-arm results and cost in `evaluation/runs/<run-id>/`.
3. SCORE — Prefer deterministic quality metrics; use a blind rubric only for nondeterministic full-evaluation items.
4. COMPARE — For full runs, compare quality, success rate, cost, time, retries, and human intervention.
5. VERDICT — Return one of `improved|neutral|regressed|inconclusive`.
6. RECORD — Store decision, reasons, suite, and evidence paths in `evaluation/reports/<run-id>.json` and the journal.
7. ACK — After each completed `targeted|full` run, call the deterministic recorder:

```text
python {{HARNESS_ROOT}}/triggers/record_self_evaluation.py {{HARNESS_ROOT}} --decision <targeted|full> --decision-file {{HARNESS_ROOT}}/evaluation/runs/<run-id>/trigger.json --verdict <improved|neutral|regressed|inconclusive>
```

The recorder validates the frozen decision, reasons, managed hashes, and `acknowledgement` failure snapshot before an atomic update. Never replace the frozen ACK decision or reasons with a rolling-metric decision that changed during evaluation. A full ACK consumes only processed reasons, pending events, and the frozen failure snapshot, then updates canonical/provider hashes, units, and cooldown. Events and failures that arrive during evaluation remain for the next boundary. A targeted ACK updates only the last decision and cooldown; it does not consume a mandatory event. This ACK prevents the same mandatory signal from reopening evaluation.

8. HANDOFF — Send a report to the improvement owner only when a full run is `regressed` or attributes a defect to the harness.

Track evaluation cost separately from operating cost, but include harness injection cost in treatment. Return `inconclusive` for insufficient samples, mismatched arm conditions, or an evaluator that did not run. Never call the recorder for an incomplete or interrupted run.
